# Third-party component licenses

SplitBox original source code is licensed under GPL-3.0-only (see LICENSE). Libraries and build tools retain their licenses; SplitBox does not claim authorship of these components.

| Component | License | Source project |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Kotlin standard library and compiler | Apache-2.0 | https://github.com/JetBrains/kotlin |
| JetBrains annotations | Apache-2.0 | https://github.com/JetBrains/java-annotations |
| kotlinx.serialization, transitive dependency | Apache-2.0 | https://github.com/Kotlin/kotlinx.serialization |
| Guava ListenableFuture, transitive dependency | Apache-2.0 | https://github.com/google/guava |
| kotlinx.coroutines | Apache-2.0 | https://github.com/Kotlin/kotlinx.coroutines |
| AndroidX Activity, Core, Lifecycle, SavedState, ProfileInstaller, Graphics Path, Compose UI/Foundation/Material 3 | Apache-2.0 | https://android.googlesource.com/platform/frameworks/support/ |
| Compose Material icons | Apache-2.0 | https://fonts.google.com/icons |
| Shizuku API и provider 13.1.5 | Apache-2.0 | https://github.com/RikkaApps/Shizuku-API |
| Android apksig | Apache-2.0 | https://android.googlesource.com/platform/tools/apksig/ |
| JUnit 4, tests only | EPL-1.0 | https://github.com/junit-team/junit4 |
| Android Gradle Plugin / SDK build tools, build only | Componentы Apache-2.0; действуют условия загрузки Android SDK | https://android.googlesource.com/ |
| Gradle, build only | Apache-2.0 | https://github.com/gradle/gradle |
| Eclipse Temurin OpenJDK, build only | GPL-2.0 with Classpath Exception | https://adoptium.net/ |
| bundletool, test fixture generation only | Apache-2.0 | https://github.com/google/bundletool |

The app does not include Google Play Services, Firebase, advertising or analytics SDKs, proprietary installers or the Shizuku server. Shizuku is a separate open source tool. ZIP, Android binary XML and protobuf parsing in core is original SplitBox code based on public Android and bundletool specifications.

Direct dependencies and versions are listed in app/build.gradle.kts and core/build.gradle.kts. To inspect the current dependency tree, run ./gradlew :app:dependencies --configuration releaseRuntimeClasspath. Transitive dependencies retain their licenses; details are available in this tree and the library source projects. Canonical Apache-2.0 and GPL-3.0 license texts are included in the app for offline reading.
